 FINDLIT*:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C FINDLIT* - find a value in the runtime constant table [M1+6]..[M1+22].
C
C Calling convention (single argument, in ACC):
C   ACC = search key
C   M1  = runtime constant-table base (P/1D)
C   M13 = return link
C
C Result:
C   ACC = offset N in 6..22 if [M1+N] equals the key (first match),
C         or 0 if none.  Key 0 matches [M1+6] and returns 6.
C
C M14 is the VLM loop index: starts at -16 (17 passes, -16..0).
C Addressing uses displacement 22, so [M1+22+M14] covers
C [M1+6]..[M1+22].  A match jumps via UZA FOUND; mismatch falls
C into VLM.  At FOUND, M14 += 22 yields the actual offset.
C===========================================================
                ,NTR,3
           15   ,ATX,1        . save key
           14   ,VTM,6-22     . 17 passes
 LOOP:     15   ,XTA,1
           14   ,UTC,
            1   ,AEX,22       . key XOR [M1+22+M14]
                ,UZA,FOUND    . match → offset
           14   ,VLM,LOOP
                ,XTA,         . not found
           13   ,UJ,
 FOUND:    14   ,UTM,22       . M14 := offset 6..22
                ,ITA,14
           13   ,UJ,
                ,END,
